2026-09-27T07:42:27.3471590Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3471917Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3472394Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3472735Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3472839Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3473064Z ================
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3473203Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3473366Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3473758Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3473981Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3474098Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3474376Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3474547Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3474684Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3475098Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3475460Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3476120Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3476634Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3476746Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3477169Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3477698Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3477977Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3478267Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3478945Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3479037Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3479242Z ========
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3479351Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3480604Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3481904Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3482119Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3482592Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3483386Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3483976Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3484553Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3550810Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3551860Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3552107Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3552567Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3552803Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3554492Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3556392Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3557404Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3559132Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:42:27.3559490Z 
